### Autoload Singleton Registrations

#### Protected File
- `wipshmup2/project.godot` (Autoload section)

#### Current Autoload Order (DO NOT CHANGE)
```ini
[autoload]

EventBus="*res://scripts/autoload/event_bus.gd"
GameState="*res://scripts/autoload/game_state.gd"
EntityFactory="*res://scripts/core/entity_factory.gd"
EnemyTemplateManager="*res://scripts/core/enemy_template_manager.gd"
BossTemplateManager="*res://scripts/core/boss_template_manager.gd"
StageTemplateManager="*res://scripts/core/stage_template_manager.gd"
```

#### Why Protected
- Load order determines dependency resolution
- Changing order can break initialization logic
- Other systems rely on these autoloads being available early
- Adding autoloads carelessly creates global state pollution

#### Rules for Adding New Autoloads
```gdscript
# ❌ DON'T add autoloads for:
- Utility functions (use static classes instead)
- Single-use managers (use composition)
- Debug/development tools (use editor plugins)
- Temporary systems (use regular nodes)

# ✅ DO add autoloads ONLY for:
- True global singletons needed everywhere
- Cross-cutting concerns (audio, input, etc.)
- Systems that must persist across scene changes

# ✅ IF adding is justified:
1. Add at END of autoload list (don't reorder)
2. Document dependencies clearly
3. Ensure no circular dependencies
4. Provide safe defaults if dependencies missing
```

#### Example: Adding an AudioManager (Acceptable)
```gdscript
# 1. Create the manager with safe defaults
# File: wipshmup2/scripts/autoload/audio_manager.gd
extends Node

func _ready() -> void:
    # Don't depend on other autoloads in _ready()
    call_deferred("_late_init")

func _late_init() -> void:
    # Safe to use other autoloads now
    EventBus.music_change_requested.connect(_on_music_change_requested)

# 2. Add to project.godot at END
[autoload]
# ... existing autoloads ...
AudioManager="*res://scripts/autoload/audio_manager.gd"  # New: Added 2025-10-18
```

