## Level 2: SENSITIVE - Modify with Caution

### Object Pooling Implementation

#### Sensitive Areas
- `EntityFactory` pool acquisition/release logic
- `reset_for_pool()` implementations in pooled entities
- Pool size configurations

#### Common Mistakes
```gdscript
# ❌ BAD: Incomplete reset leaves stale state
func reset_for_pool() -> void:
    position = Vector2.ZERO
    # Forgot to disconnect signals!
    # Forgot to reset velocity!
    # Forgot to clear references!

# ❌ BAD: Resetting too much (overhead)
func reset_for_pool() -> void:
    # Don't recreate nodes/resources
    $Sprite2D.queue_free()  # DON'T DO THIS
    var new_sprite := Sprite2D.new()
    add_child(new_sprite)

# ✅ GOOD: Complete, efficient reset
func reset_for_pool() -> void:
    # Disconnect signals
    for connection in get_incoming_connections():
        var sig: Signal = connection.signal
        if sig.is_connected(connection.callable):
            sig.disconnect(connection.callable)
    
    # Reset state
    global_position = Vector2.ZERO
    velocity = Vector2.ZERO
    health = max_health
    
    # Clear references
    target_node = null
    
    # Reset visual (reuse existing sprite)
    $Sprite2D.modulate = Color.WHITE
    visible = false
```

#### Testing Checklist for Pool Changes
- [ ] Spawn 100+ entities rapidly
- [ ] Verify all return to pool correctly
- [ ] No errors in output console
- [ ] No memory leaks (check with profiler)
- [ ] Entities reactivate correctly after pooling
- [ ] No stale state (old velocity, targets, etc.)

