### Event System Architecture

#### Sensitive Areas
- Adding new signals to `EventBus`
- Changing signal parameter types
- Removing signals

#### Rules for EventBus Signals

##### Adding New Signals (Allowed with Documentation)
```gdscript
# ✅ GOOD: Add with clear documentation and types
## Emitted when the player activates their shield ability.
## @param shield_duration: How long the shield lasts in seconds
## @param shield_strength: Damage absorption capacity
signal player_shield_activated(shield_duration: float, shield_strength: int)
```

##### Changing Signal Parameters (Requires Migration)
```gdscript
# ⚠️ BREAKING CHANGE: Requires updating all listeners
# OLD:
signal enemy_defeated(enemy_id: int, position: Vector2)

# NEW:
signal enemy_defeated(enemy_id: int, position: Vector2, score: int)

# ✅ MIGRATION STRATEGY:
# 1. Add new signal with different name
signal enemy_defeated_v2(enemy_id: int, position: Vector2, score: int)

# 2. Emit both during transition period
func _on_enemy_death() -> void:
    enemy_defeated.emit(id, pos)  # Old (deprecated)
    enemy_defeated_v2.emit(id, pos, score)  # New

# 3. Update all listeners to use v2
# 4. After all migrations, remove old signal
```

##### Removing Signals (Forbidden Without Deprecation Period)
```gdscript
# ❌ DON'T just delete
# signal old_signal()

# ✅ DO deprecate first
signal old_signal()  # DEPRECATED: Use new_signal() instead

func _emit_old_signal() -> void:
    push_warning("[EventBus] old_signal is deprecated, use new_signal")
    old_signal.emit()
```

